comment.narrative:
The total number of direct project beneficiaries includes a sum of inputs for Rwanda and Uganda as of April 2022 data since the grants/credits for both countries were completed and closed, so the latest data is reported for these 2 countries.

The DRC data is updated as of June 2022. The result for DRC shows a decrease in the number of beneficiaries during the reported quarter given the security situation in Bunagana and the panic generated at other sites.&nbsp;

The breakdown indicator for the percentage of female beneficiaries is calculated as the average of 3 countries&nbsp;inputs, following the logic as described above.&nbsp;

The result is calculated as average for data for all cross borders except Bunagana&nbsp;with the following breakdown:&nbsp;&nbsp;

Petite Barriere/Poids Lourds&nbsp; - 5 minutes

Rusizi 1 - 6 minutes&nbsp;

Kasindi/Mpondwe - 8 minutes

No data for Bunagana given the security situation since June 2022.&nbsp;

The results for this indicator and sub-indicator for gender are calculated as average for data for all cross borders except Bunagana&nbsp;with the following breakdown:&nbsp;&nbsp;

Petite Barriere/Poids Lourds&nbsp; - 19%, of which women 9%

Rusizi 1 - 0%, of which women 0%

Kasindi/Mpondwe - 35%, of which women 31%

No data for Bunagana given the security situation since June 2022.&nbsp;
